## 5. Workspace Structure

This workspace is organized around industry topics. Companies are subdirectories of their primary industry:

```text
industry/
  <industry-slug>/
    panorama/                 # Industry-level output (by skill)
      teach-in/
      industry-landscape/
      mechanism-insight/
      peer-deep-dive/
      candidate-screener/
      scenario-model/
      consensus-map/
      market-sizing/
      other/                  # Non-skill industry analysis
    companies/
      <ticker>/               # Company deep-dive — one home per company
        [YYYY-MM-DD]-*.md
        _cache/
    RESEARCH.md               # Industry overview + company registry
    _cache/
COVERAGE.md                   # Coverage source of truth (Research Tier / Alert Tier / Last Review / Next Trigger)
```

Core constraints:
- Company artifacts go in `industry/<industry>/companies/<ticker>/`
- Industry-level artifacts go in `industry/<industry>/panorama/<skill-slug>/`
- Non-skill industry analysis goes in `panorama/other/`
- Cross-industry companies are registered as references in multiple industry `index.md` files; the files themselves do not move
- `_cache/` stores source-tracked parsed materials, evidence packs, and structured data
- Topic artifact naming is resolved uniformly by `new-session`
- Workspace hooks are part of the runtime contract — do not manually edit or delete

